# ECHO — optional environment variables.
# Everything here is OPTIONAL: the app runs fully without any of them.
# Copy this file to `.env` (never commit `.env`) and fill what you need.

# ── Games catalogue (RAWG) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Free key from https://rawg.io/apidocs — no key ships in client code.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_RAWG_API_KEY=

# ── IGDB games provider (Twitch OAuth2, server proxy) ─────────────────────
# https://api-docs.igdb.com/#account-creation
# IGDB_CLIENT_ID=
# IGDB_CLIENT_SECRET=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_IGDB_ENABLED=1

# ── Trakt movies & series provider (server proxy) ──────────────────────────
# https://trakt.tv/oauth/applications
# TRAKT_CLIENT_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_TRAKT_ENABLED=1

# ── Optional Redis KV cache (server rate limiting / caching) ───────────────
# Used by lib/echo/server/kv.ts; without it the app falls back to in-memory
# caching. Free tier: https://upstash.com
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# ── Optional cloud sync (Supabase Free — username + password accounts) ────
# Everything here is OPTIONAL: the app is fully functional without sync
# (local-first; no account needed). Accounts are USERNAME + PASSWORD ONLY:
# no email address, no phone, no Google/GitHub/social sign-in, no magic
# links, and NO password recovery (a forgotten password permanently locks
# the cloud account — the UI says so before signup). Passwords are handled
# exclusively by Supabase Auth; ECHO never stores or logs them.
#
# Values are PLACEHOLDERS ONLY — never commit real keys. The owner enters
# credentials directly in the provider dashboards (never in chat).
# Supabase Free: https://supabase.com/dashboard
#
# Required Auth settings for the username adapter (see
# ECHO_HUMAN_HANDOFF/SUPABASE_SETUP.md for the full walkthrough):
#   - Confirm email: DISABLED (there is no mailbox — the internal alias uses
#     the RFC 2606 reserved .invalid domain)
#   - Email provider: enabled-by-default in Supabase but never used to send
#   - Every other provider (Google, GitHub, phone, magic link): OFF
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# Server-only. NEVER expose with NEXT_PUBLIC_. Used exclusively by the
# /api/sync/reset job path (S-2 allowlist). Enter it only in the hosting
# provider's secure environment settings.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
